<!--
  Canonical libvirt domain for win11, a Windows 11 Pro desktop VM on `bob` or `stella`.
  Define/restore with:  virsh define guests/win11/libvirt-domain.xml

  Domains here are imperative (virsh), so this file is the git-tracked source
  of truth for the VM's hardware. Keep it in sync after any `virsh edit` with:
    ssh <its host> sudo virsh dumpxml [dash][dash]inactive win11
  (double hyphen spelled out — a literal one is illegal inside an XML comment.)

  Added 2026-09-26, in the place worker5 held. It is NOT a fleet member: no
  NixOS, no comin, no k3s, no drift check. The OS inside is managed by hand
  and by Windows Update; what git owns is this hardware description and the
  answer file that installed it (autounattend.xml, beside this one).
  That is why it lives under guests/ and not hosts/: every hosts/<dir> is a
  nixosConfiguration, and emit-topology, drift-revisions, gpu-discovery and
  emit-fleet's declared-hosts check all rely on it — a Windows guest there
  would be asked over ssh for a git revision it cannot have.

  KEY CHOICES:
    - NO CARD since 2026-10-08. Until then it borrowed arcade1's RTX 3050
      (b4:00.x) and gave it back through arcade-ctl whenever arcade1 started.
      Without a passed-through device it can move live between bob and
      stella (vm-move, modules/vm-host.nix), and the 3050 is arcade1's alone until
      it goes to stella's host for k3s. The desktop is the QXL screen below.
    - ALWAYS ON, the owner's call (2026-10-08). labo.vmHost.alwaysOn on bob
      and stella: whichever host defines it saves it on shutdown and resumes
      it on boot. Defined on ONE host at a time; vm-move carries the
      definition and the autostart flag.
    - 6 vCPU / 12 GiB (16 until 2026-10-08: without a card, and always on,
      it makes room for coquille beside it on bob's 48 GB). 6 vCPU leaves the
      other 6 of a W-2135's 12 threads to whatever shares its host. Topology 3 cores x 2 threads MUST multiply to <vcpu>
      or libvirt refuses the domain, and only at start, not at define.
    - TPM 2.0 (swtpm, `virtualisation.libvirtd.qemu.swtpm.enable`, on bob and stella)
      because Windows 11 setup requires one. Secure Boot is OFF, like every
      other guest here: nixpkgs ships no OVMF vars with Microsoft's keys
      enrolled, so the answer file sets LabConfig\BypassSecureBootCheck
      instead. The TPM state lives in /var/lib/libvirt/swtpm/<uuid> — keep
      the uuid below stable or BitLocker-style TPM bindings are lost.
    - CPU host-passthrough, MIGRATABLE (2026-10-08). With migratable='off'
      the guest also gets invtsc, and libvirt refuses a live move ("State
      blocked by non-migratable CPU device (invtsc flag)") — the first
      vm-move of win11 hit exactly that. bob and stella are the same W-2135.
    - Hyper-V enlightenments + hypervclock: the standard Windows-guest set.
      THE RTC IS UTC, and Windows is told so (HKLM\...\TimeZoneInformation
      RealTimeIsUniversal = 1, set by win11-setup.ps1) — the Linux convention,
      which no DST change or host setting can shift. Two wrong turns first
      (2026-09-26), both leaving Windows four hours ahead with the right zone:
      `localtime` is the HOST's local time, and stella runs in UTC; then
      offset='timezone' timezone='America/Toronto', which libvirt turns into
      `-rtc base=localtime` with TZ=America/Toronto in QEMU's environment —
      but NixOS keeps zone files in /etc/zoneinfo, QEMU gets no TZDIR, and
      glibc falls back to UTC without a word. Takes effect on a full
      stop/start of the domain, not a guest reboot.
    - virtio disk and NIC. Setup has no driver for either, so the answer file
      loads viostor/NetKVM from the virtio-win drive in windowsPE and installs
      virtio-win-guest-tools.exe (all drivers + qemu guest agent) at first
      logon. The agent is what lets `virsh shutdown` use [dash][dash]mode agent; ACPI
      works regardless, Windows honours the power button.
    - Single NIC, macvtap on the host's `vlan10` (same name on bob and stella), static 192.0.2.143/23,
      IPv4 ONLY — the same NDP/DAD reflection on stella's macvtap that forced
      IPv6 off the arcades would make Windows flag its own address duplicate.
      The answer file unbinds IPv6 from the adapter.
    - QXL is the only screen: vgamem 32 MiB for 1920x1080x32 (16 MiB held
      1024x768 only). QEMU console on <host>.lab.example:5903 (LAN + VPN only),
      whichever host runs it; TightVNC inside on win11:5900.
-->
<domain type='kvm'>
  <name>win11</name>
  <uuid>00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000</uuid>
  <memory unit='KiB'>12582912</memory>
  <currentMemory unit='KiB'>12582912</currentMemory>
  <vcpu placement='static'>6</vcpu>
  <os firmware='efi'>
    <type arch='x86_64' machine='q35'>hvm</type>
    <firmware>
      <feature enabled='no' name='enrolled-keys'/>
      <feature enabled='no' name='secure-boot'/>
    </firmware>
    <loader readonly='yes' type='pflash' format='raw'>/run/libvirt/nix-ovmf/edk2-x86_64-code.fd</loader>
    <nvram template='/run/libvirt/nix-ovmf/edk2-i386-vars.fd' templateFormat='raw' format='raw'>/var/lib/libvirt/qemu/nvram/win11_VARS.fd</nvram>
    <boot dev='hd'/>
    <boot dev='cdrom'/>
  </os>
  <features>
    <acpi/>
    <apic/>
    <hyperv mode='custom'>
      <relaxed state='on'/>
      <vapic state='on'/>
      <spinlocks state='on' retries='8191'/>
      <vpindex state='on'/>
      <runtime state='on'/>
      <synic state='on'/>
      <stimer state='on'/>
      <reset state='on'/>
      <frequencies state='on'/>
      <tlbflush state='on'/>
      <ipi state='on'/>
    </hyperv>
  </features>
  <cpu mode='host-passthrough' check='none' migratable='on'>
    <topology sockets='1' dies='1' cores='3' threads='2'/>
  </cpu>
  <clock offset='utc'>
    <timer name='rtc' tickpolicy='catchup'/>
    <timer name='pit' tickpolicy='delay'/>
    <timer name='hpet' present='no'/>
    <timer name='hypervclock' present='yes'/>
  </clock>
  <on_poweroff>destroy</on_poweroff>
  <on_reboot>restart</on_reboot>
  <on_crash>destroy</on_crash>
  <pm>
    <suspend-to-mem enabled='no'/>
    <suspend-to-disk enabled='no'/>
  </pm>
  <devices>
    <emulator>/run/libvirt/nix-emulators/qemu-system-x86_64</emulator>
    <disk type='file' device='disk'>
      <driver name='qemu' type='qcow2' discard='unmap' cache='none' io='native'/>
      <source file='/var/lib/libvirt/images/win11.qcow2'/>
      <target dev='vda' bus='virtio'/>
    </disk>
    <!-- Empty cdroms once installed. To reinstall, insert the Windows ISO in
         sda and the answer-file + virtio-win ISO in sdb:
           virsh change-media win11 sda /var/lib/libvirt/images/win11-install.iso
           virsh change-media win11 sdb /var/lib/libvirt/images/win11-drivers.iso
         The Windows boot loader waits for a key ("Press any key to boot from
         CD or DVD") and falls through to the disk if none comes, so send one
         right after start: virsh send-key win11 KEY_ENTER. -->
    <disk type='file' device='cdrom'>
      <driver name='qemu' type='raw'/>
      <target dev='sda' bus='sata'/>
      <readonly/>
    </disk>
    <disk type='file' device='cdrom'>
      <driver name='qemu' type='raw'/>
      <target dev='sdb' bus='sata'/>
      <readonly/>
    </disk>
    <controller type='pci' index='0' model='pcie-root'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='1' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='2' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='3' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='4' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='5' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='6' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='7' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='pci' index='8' model='pcie-root-port'/>
    <controller type='sata' index='0'/>
    <controller type='virtio-serial' index='0'/>
    <controller type='usb' index='0' model='qemu-xhci'/>

    <!-- VLAN10 (fleet mgmt, default route). Only interface. -->
    <interface type='direct' trustGuestRxFilters='yes'>
      <mac address='02:00:00:00:00:01'/>
      <source dev='vlan10' mode='bridge'/>
      <model type='virtio'/>
    </interface>

    <channel type='unix'>
      <target type='virtio' name='org.qemu.guest_agent.0'/>
    </channel>
    <tpm model='tpm-crb'>
      <backend type='emulator' version='2.0'/>
    </tpm>
    <input type='tablet' bus='usb'/>
    <input type='mouse' bus='ps2'/>
    <input type='keyboard' bus='ps2'/>
    <graphics type='vnc' port='-1' autoport='yes' listen='127.0.0.1'/>
    <video>
      <model type='qxl' ram='65536' vram='65536' vgamem='32768' heads='1'/>
    </video>
    <audio id='1' type='none'/>
    <memballoon model='virtio'/>
  </devices>
</domain>
